{"body":"[P1] The streaming loop now performs a sequence of independent LIMIT/OFFSET queries, but the repository queries order only by non-unique timestamps/created_at and are not run under a stable snapshot/high-water mark. If tied rows straddle a page boundary, or if ingestion inserts matching rows while an export is running, rows can move between offsets and the artifact can skip or duplicate records. The old path was a single SELECT and did not have this cross-page correctness issue. Please make export pagination snapshot-stable and total-order deterministic, for example with (order_col, id) keyset pagination plus a captured high-water mark, or a repeatable-read transaction plus ORDER BY ..., dt.id.","commit_id":"cced4e390d934cb9e2d97a3ebe830029fd78088f","created_at":"2026-04-16T15:58:36Z","id":3094574121,"in_reply_to":null,"line":null,"original_line":219,"path":"api/src/export_stream.rs","user":"user1303836"}
{"body":"[P1] write_export_to_file streams straight to the final exports/{job_id}.{ext} path, but heartbeat lease loss only stops the heartbeat task; it does not cancel this awaited write. A stale worker that resumes after claim_export_job reassigns the job can keep truncating/writing the same path as the new owner, and the error cleanup below can remove the new owner's artifact. update_or_abort catches the lost lease only after these side effects. Please propagate a lease-lost cancellation token into the page loop and/or write to attempt-scoped temp files and atomically publish only after an ownership-guarded transition.","commit_id":"ea3144756f3798f007b1f5e71c2c098c111013a7","created_at":"2026-04-16T15:58:36Z","id":3094574126,"in_reply_to":null,"line":255,"original_line":207,"path":"api/src/export_worker.rs","user":"user1303836"}
{"body":"[P2] CSV headers are only emitted inside write_page, but this break happens before write_page when the first page is empty. That turns an empty CSV export into a zero-byte file; the previous *_to_csv helpers always returned the header row, and CSV consumers rely on that schema even with zero records. Emit the header once before paging for CSV, or special-case total == 0 before flushing.","commit_id":"cced4e390d934cb9e2d97a3ebe830029fd78088f","created_at":"2026-04-16T15:58:36Z","id":3094574129,"in_reply_to":null,"line":null,"original_line":230,"path":"api/src/export_stream.rs","user":"user1303836"}
{"body":"[P2] Sink-backed exports still read the whole artifact into memory before delivery, so any job with sink_config can still hit the OOM class this change is meant to remove. The row cap is not a byte cap, especially for event_details/raw JSON datasets. If this is intentionally a follow-up, I would avoid calling the export worker memory-bounded for sink jobs; otherwise the sink trait should accept a file path/stream so delivery preserves the bounded-memory property too.","commit_id":"cced4e390d934cb9e2d97a3ebe830029fd78088f","created_at":"2026-04-16T15:58:36Z","id":3094574135,"in_reply_to":null,"line":null,"original_line":279,"path":"api/src/export_worker.rs","user":"user1303836"}
{"body":"[P1] This send is not cancellation-aware. If the disk writer fails while the channel is full, write_export_to_file cancels the token and awaits the producer task, but page_rx is still alive and no longer being polled, so this send can wait forever. That leaves the export job heartbeating and the REPEATABLE READ transaction open instead of failing/cleaning up. Please make the send a tokio::select! against cancel.cancelled(), or explicitly drop the receiver before awaiting the producer after a write-loop error.","commit_id":"ea3144756f3798f007b1f5e71c2c098c111013a7","created_at":"2026-04-16T16:43:22Z","id":3094852491,"in_reply_to":null,"line":1268,"original_line":1268,"path":"adapters/src/v2_repo.rs","user":"user1303836"}
{"body":"[P1] The no-sink path still publishes before a lease-guarded DB update. If this worker has been reclaimed but its heartbeat has not observed Ok(false) yet, it can rename its temp file over the canonical artifact; when the subsequent update_or_abort returns false, best_effort_unlink(final_path) can also delete the new owner's artifact. Please use the same lease-confirming pre-publish transition as the sink path, or another ownership-guarded publish step, before renaming to the canonical path.","commit_id":"ea3144756f3798f007b1f5e71c2c098c111013a7","created_at":"2026-04-16T16:43:22Z","id":3094852495,"in_reply_to":null,"line":465,"original_line":465,"path":"api/src/export_worker.rs","user":"user1303836"}

